### ===========================================================================
### Clinic Booking API: requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension
### (extension id: humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above any request.
###
### SETUP
###  1. Make sure your .env (same folder as this file) has API_KEY=...
###  2. Change @baseUrl to your Render URL to test the deployed app.
###  3. Run the sections IN ORDER from the top. Section 1 resets the data.
###  4. Each email may only make 5 booking attempts per minute (Level 5),
###     so the sections use different emails. If you rerun, wait a minute.
### ===========================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@apiKey = {{$dotenv API_KEY}}


### ===========================================================================
### 0. HEALTH (no API key needed)
### ===========================================================================
GET {{baseUrl}}/health


### ===========================================================================
### 1. LEVEL 1: reset, list, book, look up
### ===========================================================================

### 1.1 Reset: delete all bookings and replace all slots (expect 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slots": [
    { "id": "s1", "provider": "Dr Ade", "start": "2027-12-10T09:00:00Z", "end": "2027-12-10T09:30:00Z" },
    { "id": "s2", "provider": "Dr Ade", "start": "2027-12-10T09:30:00Z", "end": "2027-12-10T10:00:00Z" },
    { "id": "s3", "provider": "Dr Ade", "start": "2027-12-10T10:00:00Z", "end": "2027-12-10T10:30:00Z" },
    { "id": "s4", "provider": "Dr Okafor", "start": "2027-12-10T10:30:00Z", "end": "2027-12-10T11:00:00Z" },
    { "id": "s5", "provider": "Dr Okafor", "start": "2027-12-10T11:00:00Z", "end": "2027-12-10T11:30:00Z" },
    { "id": "s6", "provider": "Dr Okafor", "start": "2027-12-10T11:30:00Z", "end": "2027-12-10T12:00:00Z" },
    { "id": "past1", "provider": "Dr Ade", "start": "2020-01-01T09:00:00Z", "end": "2020-01-01T09:30:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 1.1b Add MORE slots without wiping anything (extra endpoint, expect 201; id is optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/slots
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slots": [
    { "provider": "Felix White", "start": "2027-12-11T09:00:00Z", "end": "2027-12-11T09:30:00Z" },
    { "provider": "Dora Star", "start": "2027-12-11T09:30:00Z", "end": "2027-12-11T10:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 1.2 List slots: earliest start first, every slot has "available": true (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/slots
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 1.3 List slots for one provider only (expect 200, only Dr Ade)
GET {{baseUrl}}/slots?provider=Dr Ade
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 1.4 Book s1 (expect 201, status "confirmed"). The id is saved for later requests.
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slot_id": "a260e122-eba3-410d-b3dd-4960c88f5a98",
  "name": "Queen Esther",
  "email": "esther@gmail.com"
}

### 1.5 Look up that booking (expect 200, same booking)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 1.6 List slots again: s1 should now say "available": false
GET {{baseUrl}}/slots
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 1.7 Look up a booking that doesn't exist (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/does-not-exist
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}


### ===========================================================================
### 2. LEVEL 2: API key and validation
### ===========================================================================

### 2.1 No API key (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/slots

### 2.2 Wrong API key (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/slots
X-API-Key: wrong-key

### 2.3 Booking without a key (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s2", "name": "No Key", "email": "nokey@example.com" }

### 2.4 Empty name (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s2", "name": "", "email": "val@example.com" }

### 2.5 Missing slot_id (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Val Idator", "email": "val@example.com" }

### 2.6 Invalid email (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s2", "name": "Val Idator", "email": "not-an-email" }

### 2.7 Name is only spaces (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s2", "name": "     ", "email": "val2@example.com" }

### 2.8 Broken JSON (expect 400, {"error": "body is not valid JSON"})
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s2", "name": 

### 2.9 Slot doesn't exist (expect 404, "slot not found")
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "nope", "name": "Lost Patient", "email": "lost@example.com" }

### 2.10 Slot already started (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "past1", "name": "Too Late", "email": "late@example.com" }

### 2.11 Spaces trimmed, email lower-cased (expect 201: name "Bola Ade", email "bola@example.com")
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s2", "name": "   Bola Ade   ", "email": "  BOLA@Example.com  " }


### ===========================================================================
### 3. LEVEL 3: no double booking, and cancelling
### (for the "many requests at the same moment" test run: npm run race)
### ===========================================================================

### 3.1 Someone else tries s1, which Ada already booked (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Late Larry", "email": "larry@example.com" }

### 3.2 Cancel Ada's booking (expect 200, status "cancelled")
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 3.3 Cancel it again (expect 409, already cancelled)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 3.4 Cancel a booking that doesn't exist (expect 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/does-not-exist
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 3.5 The cancelled slot is free again: Larry can now book s1 (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Late Larry", "email": "larry@example.com" }

### 3.6 Ada's cancelled booking still exists with status "cancelled" (expect 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{createBooking.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}


### ===========================================================================
### 4. LEVEL 4: retries (Idempotency-Key) and pagination
### ===========================================================================

### 4.1 First request with a key (expect 201)
# @name idemFirst
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{ "slot_id": "s3", "name": "Ida Mpotent", "email": "idem@example.com" }

### 4.2 SAME key, SAME body (expect 201 again, SAME booking id, header Idempotent-Replayed: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{ "slot_id": "s3", "name": "Ida Mpotent", "email": "idem@example.com" }

### 4.3 SAME key, DIFFERENT body (expect 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-001

{ "slot_id": "s3", "name": "Someone Else", "email": "idem@example.com" }

### 4.4 Slot s3 has exactly one booking: check it
GET {{baseUrl}}/slots
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### --- pagination: create 3 bookings for one email ---

### 4.5 Pager booking 1 (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s4", "name": "Page Turner", "email": "pager@example.com" }

### 4.6 Pager booking 2 (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s5", "name": "Page Turner", "email": "pager@example.com" }

### 4.7 Pager booking 3 (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s6", "name": "Page Turner", "email": "pager@example.com" }

### 4.8 Page 1: limit=2 (expect 2 bookings, oldest first, a next_cursor)
# @name page1
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com&limit=2
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.9 Page 2: send next_cursor back as cursor (expect 1 booking, next_cursor null)
# @name page2
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com&limit=2&cursor={{page1.response.body.next_cursor}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.10 Email match ignores case (expect the same bookings as 4.8)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=PAGER@Example.COM&limit=2
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.11 Default limit is 10 (expect all 3 bookings, next_cursor null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.12 Email with no bookings (expect 200, empty list, next_cursor null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=nobody@example.com
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.13 limit=0 (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com&limit=0
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.14 limit=51 (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com&limit=51
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.15 limit=abc (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com&limit=abc
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.16 Garbage cursor (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings?email=pager@example.com&cursor=!!!
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 4.17 Missing email (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}


### ===========================================================================
### 5. LEVEL 5: spam protection (max 5 attempts per email per minute)
### Send 5.1 to 5.6 quickly, within one minute. Failed attempts count too:
### all of these hit an already-booked slot, so 5.1 to 5.5 return 409.
### ===========================================================================

### 5.1 Attempt 1 (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }

### 5.2 Attempt 2 (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }

### 5.3 Attempt 3 (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }

### 5.4 Attempt 4 (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }

### 5.5 Attempt 5 (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }

### 5.6 Attempt 6 (expect 429 and a Retry-After header in seconds)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }

### 5.7 Same email, different capitalisation is the SAME person (expect 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "SPAM@example.com" }

### 5.8 A different email is NOT affected (expect 409 from the slot, not 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Innocent", "email": "innocent@example.com" }

### 5.9 Wait for the Retry-After seconds, then send again (expect 409 again, not 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slot_id": "s1", "name": "Spammer", "email": "spam@example.com" }


### ===========================================================================
### 6. RESET AGAIN: wipes everything so you can rerun all sections
### ===========================================================================
POST {{baseUrl}}/reset
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slots": [] }
